% ============================================================================
% wave-properties.query.adj — a worked recall over the physics wave-properties
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does frequency
% measure?": it states no physics fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `wave_property` rows and returns the definition + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% definition `time_for_one_cycle`, recall its property — period). A word that is
% not one of the four measurable wave properties abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a definition.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli wave-properties.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "wave-properties.adj"

? wave_property(wavelength, $Definition)   % expect distance_between_identical_parts
? wave_property(frequency, $Definition)    % expect waves_per_second
? wave_property(amplitude, $Definition)    % expect max_displacement_from_rest
? wave_property($Property, time_for_one_cycle) % reverse bind — expect period
? wave_property(color, $Definition)        % expect abstain — color is a perception that depends on wavelength, not itself a measurable property of the wave
